    "title": "Tarris Reed Jr. – NBA Draft Room",
    "text": "NBA DRAFT SCOUTING REPORTPOSITION: CFROM: UConnHT: 6-10WT: 260BORN: NAYEAR: Sr.WING: NAREACH: NADraft NotesTarris Reed Jr. is a burly, tough, below the rim big man who plays with an edge. He’s got really good strength and knows how to use it. He’s an excellent rebounder, screen setter and has good touch around the rim.He knows his role and does all the dirty work on the court.He’s not a run/jump athlete and isn’t a great rim protector but he impacts the game in many ways with his size, strength and toughness.ComparisonsNADraft Projectionlate first to second round pick in the 2026 NBA DraftLatest Big BoardVideos 2026 Center RankingsAday Mara – 7-3 – Michigan (Spain)Chris Cenac Jr. – 6-10 – HoustonMotiejus Krivas – 7-2 – Arizona (Lithuania)Morez Johnson – 6-10 – MichiganHenri Veesaar – 7-0 – North Carolina (Estonia)Jayden Quaintance – 6-10 – KentuckyTarris Reed Jr. – 6-10 – UConnMor Massamba Diop – 7-1 – Arizona State (Senegal)Flory Bidunga – 6-10 – Kansas (Congo)Patrick Ngongba II – 6-10 – DukeZuby Ejiofor – 6-9 – St. John’sMouhamed Faye – 6-10 – Reggio Emilio (Senegal)Keba Keita – 6-8 – BYU (Mali)Rafael Castro – 6-11 – George WashingtonAaron Bradshaw – 7-1 – MemphisUgonna Kingsley Onyenso – 7-0 – Kansas State (Nigeria)Oswin Erhunmunse – 6-9 – Providence (Nigeria)Felix Okpara – 6-11 – Tennessee (Nigeria)Oscar Cluff – 6-11 – PurdueVincent Iwuchukwu – 7-0 – GeorgetownRobbie Avila – 6-10 – Saint Louis",
